  "implementation": [
    "Each process page/ASID owner now owns real DirectClient/DirectSubmit workspace in separately allocated storage;small OSObject keeps genuine object/page/domain/connection references,not synthetic handles",
    "Existing beginKernelIo follows actual execution grant+OOB+drain with prepare->exact ASID authorization/select->real VM attach->client/submit open;existing kernel-only IOUserClient really reaches this chain",
    "Existing dispatch,CPU mapping-token view and CPU-unmap lease paths use the real per-connection client. Fixed method/input/output checks and success-only reply copy retained. Imported task remains kernel_task;ordinary apps not admitted",
    "Actual process submit jobs/fences are drained before root switching;nonselected process with outstanding/poisoned work refuses. No use of kernel-submit emptiness as a process completion proof. Real existing A7XX context reset producer requested on successful switches/new client",
    "Normal IO close drains real jobs,releaseAll actual BOs,closes client and submit,frees their CPU workspace,restores kernel TTBR,detaches seed-only VM metadata,ASID-TLBSYNC/page release,then original execution/OOB window release;each stage only after real previous success",
    "Intrusive process-list node removed before retirement can destroy it;only surviving failed partial is reinserted. Dispatch snapshot retains actual OSObject across close and revalidates under same issuer;new dispatch rejected after close begins",
    "Any failure retains remaining resource state and stops;no automatic reset,rollback,failed-context restore or retry"
  ],
